 "text": " In the early days of Artificial Intelligence, researchers tried to build robots that work like Trace Grandmaster, scan the room, build a complete 3D model of every train, and work in memory, plan a path, and finally move one step. The result? If someone walked past the robot, the robot froze for minutes trying to recalculate its giant world model. Then, in the 1918th, Robotic Ronit Brooks asked a simple question. How does an insect dodge a water in milliseconds with a brain smaller than the spec of dodge? The answer launched Behaviourist AI. Welcome to Uniship Dodge. In this tutorial, you will learn how retips agents act in real-time using the scenes, design, artgroups, how layer-sumption architecture keeps robots safe, how QI learning lets an agent learn from regrets and mistakes, and how hardware, networks, and AI combine into one complex system.",
